/* book Worked example 2: Q: Estimate the drift-layer thickness needed to block 1200 V in silicon (Ec = 0.3 MV/cm), SiC (2.2 MV/cm) and GaN (3 MV/cm).
   1. Silicon: W = 2 × 1200 ÷ (0.3 × 106) = 8.0 × 10−3 cm = 80 µm.
   2. SiC: W = 2 × 1200 ÷ (2.2 × 106) = 1.09 × 10−3 cm = 10.9 µm.
   3. GaN: W = 2 × 1200 ÷ (3 × 106) = 8.0 × 10−4 cm = 8 µm.
   4. Silicon needs 80 ÷ 10.9 ≈ 7.3 times the SiC thickness, and its layer must also be far more lightly doped, so its resistance is much higher.
   Answer: About 80 µm for Si, 10.9 µm for SiC and 8 µm for GaN. */
